Z||000013||artherd||12-06-2001||05:36 PM||||I actually really like the Jalapeno.<P>If I ever built one though it would have to have AWD added on and have an axel gear drive somewhat like a Hummer uses.<P>Still, look at that ground clearance combined with a very low CG would make for an off-roading maven<P>PS: those 20s would do for some light offroading (like if you live on a gravel/dirt driveway) just fine methinks.  They shod them with fairly tall tyres. \<P>Then again, my N* is getting 35 series (265/35/18) so I'll be quiet now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm sure it needs the mudgobbers for any real offroading though.  I'd put the Jalapeno up against a Land rover any day, I wouldn't waste time with any 'fad' suvs.<P>At least it's the best looking 'SUV' made...<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000014||88-DOHC||12-06-2001||05:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>Did Pontiac have a few extra parts around, get high and then put together the Aztec?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> <P>I can't believe people are buying that!!!<P><BR>Uggghhh!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>between the Aztec, Avalanche, and the new Lincoln (I think its the Lincoln), I am seriously wondering what the GM designers are smoking.  All have that boxy body with "chevron" like front ends and are all very...very.. fugly.  <P>Back when GM first had the Aztec on the car show circuit they were showing off another vehicle design at the same time. Auto analyst's gave praise to that design and were disgusted with the Aztec. So which one did GM build.... Yep, the one everyone hated, the Aztec. :/<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mark Matthews||12-06-2001||06:12 PM||||well, I'd have to disagree with you on Jalapeno vs. Land Rover.  I like the Jalapeno and all, and I'm gonna do the kit, but a land rover would SMOKE the Jalapeno.  The Land Rover can withhold a 38 degree angle and still drive on all four tires!  My boss has one, that thing is the bomb!<P>I still don't think anything could ever beat an old Jeep Willy's.  Those things are damn mountain goats.  I used to have a FJ40 Land Cruiser.  I've done my fourwheeling.  I just like the look of the Jalapeno.  The high stance would also mean I could drive to the local supermarket and not get highcentered on a speed bump!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  JM2C<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir||||reg||1
Z||000016||Black86SE||12-06-2001||07:17 PM||||I think the Avalanches look like a small scavenger dinosaur. Like a compy. I saw something the other day that looked like an Avalanche but I think it was a Caddy. Do they have their own version of the Avalanche? I know Lincoln Blackwood is sorta like that but it doesn't have the plastic.||||reg||1
Z||000017||BN Boomer||12-07-2001||03:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B> I'd put the Jalapeno up against a Land rover any day, I wouldn't waste time with any 'fad' suvs.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And you'd immediately have the distinct displeasure of having your a$$ handed to you on a platter.<P>I agree that most SUVs these days are "fads" and posers. But the Land Rovers are not. Even a stock Defender 90 is an incredibly competent offroad machine.<P>For what it would cost to build a Fiero into even a mild offroad machine, you could build up an older Jeep CJ that would absolutely slaughter the Fiero in every aspect of offroading. I hope that Jalapeno kit includes some underbody armor. The long, exposed, and relatively fragile coolant lines of the Fiero would not last long in an offroad environment harsher than a gravel road or the speedbump at Starbucks.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Nashco||12-07-2001||03:31 AM||||Yup, I back up the Land Rover claim...Land Rovers really do have excellent off roading capabilities for out-of-the-box performance.  If you laugh at this, check out their latest vehicles.  They have some very impressive features, along with many gadgets built particularly for off road functions.  Cool vehicles if you ask me...just not in my price range for something with lower miles <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
